// =============================================================================
// Chora LangGraph Orchestrator Service (gRPC)
// =============================================================================
//
// Source-of-truth: docs/architecture-review-inputs-2026-05-07.md Tier 2 D5,
//   Tier 5 D20 (hybrid crew composition)
//   + .claude/skills/langgraph-orchestrator-python/SKILL.md
//   + .claude/skills/crew-composition/SKILL.md
//   + memory project_chora_data_plane.md, project_chora_governance_ai.md
//
// Python LangGraph orchestrator's gRPC API for cross-domain crews and
// complex multi-agent workflows. Always-on, leader-elected, stateful via
// PostgresSaver checkpointer in chora_ai_kernel database.
//
// Hybrid crew composition (Tier 5 D20):
//   - FIXED_CORE_PER_DOMAIN: each Content {verb} domain has a fixed core crew
//     (e.g., Creation = 6-agent gate: Validator → Classifier → Web Researcher
//      → Q&A Generator → Evaluator → Reporter)
//   - DYNAMIC_SPECIALIST: specialist agents summoned on-demand per workflow
//
// Two RPC shapes:
//   - RunCrew: kick off a crew (fixed core or dynamic specialist) — returns
//     the final result synchronously when the workflow completes
//   - StreamCrewProgress: observe an in-flight crew run (planning / dispatching
//     / executing / compiling / finalizing)
//
// Deployed in chora-local team-platform (Team 3 owns kernel orchestrators);
// per-domain orchestrators in domain projects (Team 1 / Team 2 own domain
// orchestrators).
//
// mTLS via the service mesh; SPIFFE identity in mesh.
// =============================================================================

